{"evt":"summary_set","id":"note:note-mqjdz46xm7b","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","summary":"APPROVE. Commit 98591c0 correctly fixes false-positive redirect detection in hooks/orch-gate-bash.sh by computing CMD_REDIR via sed masking of single- and double-quoted spans to placeholder 'Q'. Scope is minimal (4 lines added, 2 grep invocations repointed); all other write-pattern checks remain on raw $CMD. The placeholder-not-deletion approach preserves detection of real redirects to quoted filenames. Four verify-fix.sh cases are meaningful and pass. Minor style divergence (verify uses [[:space:]] vs production \\s) is harmless on GNU grep. The fix logic was successfully carried forward into hooks/lib/gate-policy.js:hasBashWritePattern during the subsequent unification refactor (commit e2cf93b), where it uses equivalent JS regex. Attempt branch was already manually merged to main (c0142f4) before this judge task ran; merge_attempt returned branch-not-found but the code is confirmed in HEAD.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-18T19:47:41.509Z"}
